// B4 (2026-09-30): the SEQUENCE FANOUT. `fanout(f, xs)` applies `f` to each
// element as an independent branch and collects the results in order; with
// no schedule installed it runs sequentially and IS `map` — the prelude
// declares it as exactly that, so this leg is the VALUES control (boot
// 6f2ce437 runs it through the prelude's body once the declaration
// exists); the schedule's witness is mn-fanout-seq-threaded.
// Expected exit: 12.
fn main() = match fanout({ x => x * 2 }, [1, 2, 3]) {
  [a, b, c] => a + b + c,
  _ => 0,
}
